# threed (Cursor rules export)

The condensed form of the `threed` skill — the full skill lives at github.com/lucasgabrieldevgg/threed; this file carries the operating rules.

## The threed contract

1. Purpose decides everything: destination sets budget (game 10–50k tris, web <100k, print sane), format (GLB/FBX/STL/3MF/USDZ), and gates. No purpose → ask.
2. Know the size before you build or generate. Real units declared up front; bounding box verified against intent. Scale is the #1 AI-3D failure.
3. Silhouette before detail. Blockout → rendered silhouette check → then detail. Detail on wrong proportions is scheduled rework.
4. The mesh is data: manifold, oriented, scaled, budgeted — each property gated with numbers (trimesh), not vibes.
5. Two-channel verification: numbers (watertight, winding, volume, extents, faces) AND fixed-view renders the agent actually inspects. Script success ≠ model success.
6. Every export gets a roundtrip: reimport, probe counts/UVs/materials/scale, render one check.

## Path matrix

- Exact dimensions/holes → CAD code (OpenSCAD CSG, CadQuery parametric). Don't sculpt a bracket.
- Organic from reference → Blender headless, gated phases. Don't CAD a dragon.
- Textured asset fast → generation API, concept-image-first → repair + decimate (draft, never final).
- Convert/optimize/validate → trimesh + gltf-transform (+ Blender for cross-format).
- Printing → printability gates + orientation + user presses Print.

## Hard rules

- Never claim a model from code success or file existence — numbers + renders or it didn't happen.
- AI meshes are drafts: analyze + repair (merge verts → remove degenerate → fix normals, IN THAT ORDER) + decimate to budget; check volume delta (repair that removes >5% volume amputated something).
- Price before spend: quote/dry-run first; approval gates between costly stages; one variable per rerun; regenerate the failing view, not the asset.
- Quads live in FBX/DCC only — glTF/OBJ/STL are triangles; never promise quad topology in a GLB.
- Scale, pivot, normals drift between pipeline steps — re-verify after every stage.
- STL/OBJ are unitless (slicer assumes mm); glTF is meters; 3MF carries units. Trust the imported bounding box, not API self-reports.
- The print button belongs to the user; the agent delivers analysis, orientation, preview, manifest.
- Builds are numbered idempotent scripts (00_init → 10_blockout → … → 50_export), never hand edits. Seeds fixed. Constants commented with their source.
- .blend is not interchange — exports + manifest are the deliverable.

## The gates (trimesh)

```python
import trimesh
m = trimesh.load(path, force="mesh")
# watertight, winding_consistent, volume > 0, extents vs intent, face count vs budget
# repair order: merge_vertices → remove_degenerate_faces → fix_normals → re-gate
```

## Review renders

clay (silhouette/mass) · silhouette (pure shape) · wire (topology) · checker (UVs) · turntable 16×22.5° (every face a frame) · reference-matched camera (drift measurable). Workbench for speed; gameplay pixel size for "does this detail even exist". Contact sheet, look at it, regenerate only failing views.

## Slop death list (cut on sight)

Non-manifold "done" · inverted normals · unitless scale · detail before silhouette · smooth-everything · export never reimported · z-fighting coincident faces · one blob where spec said parts · placeholder dimensions · 4K textures on 128px assets · quads promised in GLB · unverified repair · "PBR" that is one flat color · viewport claims.

